ody  showing that they pull from the dark  dimension there's also a highlight of  red aka chaos magic and it hammers on  the idea that this version pulls from a  number of energies in order to cast his  spells it's some amazing attention to  detail that really adds to the episode  and also his character as a whole now  the watcher looks on but says he won't  interfere like you when you see an  argument playing out in the comments  section on facebook now i do actually  think that the watcher will interfere at  some point and that this will break  reality open which will cause carnage in  the hyundai sponsorship advert for the  show we did see him as part of the fight  and this line here just sticks out like  a sore thumb now we see as strange sucks  the life out of everyone like my  mother-in-law and he turns his attention  to a version of gora and absorbs it too  it is important to bear in mind that  this is an alternate version to the one  that we saw in what if episode 1 and  thus it isn't the one that peggy fought  and therefore the character can return  he finds obeng on his yoda death bed and  it's revealed that he's actually allowed  this to play out because he's only half  a man and therefore cannot be  all-powerful we cut back to the other  half of strange sat in the sanctuarium  but rather than ignoring wong's warnings  he takes his guidance it's revealed that  when strange travelled into the past  that the ancient one actually split him  into two and had one version remain  behind whilst the other one went to the  library this darker version has been  feasting on the universe and the only  way to stop him is for the lighter one  to take him down it brings a whole new  meaning to the phrase your own worst  enemy and outside the sanctorum strange  finds his reality being absorbed and  taken over by a black mold that  envelopes new york i've got a lot of  flashes here of spider-man web of  shadows in which the symbiotes took over  the city and though it's un